# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project 7 — what does and does not belong in version control.
#
# Principle: track everything we wrote, and nothing a script can rebuild.
# Every excluded dataset is recoverable with the download scripts, so a fresh
# clone plus `download_data.sh` reproduces the full tree.
#
# Two things are excluded for reasons other than size:
#   - Journal PDFs and publisher supplementary files are copyrighted. They are
#     not ours to redistribute, even in a private repo.
#   - Derived tables extracted from those supplementary files are likewise left
#     out; `01_extract_ground_truth.py` regenerates them in seconds.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- raw and derived data (regenerable) ---
**/data/raw/
**/data/processed/
**/data/reference/
**/data/external/
**/data/cohort_*/
*.tsv.gz
*.txt.gz
*.gtf.gz
mixture_TPM_*.txt

# --- generated outputs ---
**/results/
**/outputs/
**/out/

# --- copyrighted third-party material ---
# Papers and publisher supplementary files. Cite them; don't redistribute them.
**/paper/
**/data/supplementary/
*.pdf

# Extracted full text of copyrighted papers
**/docs/*fulltext*.txt
**/docs/supplementary_methods.txt

# --- caches and editor cruft ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.venv/
venv/

# --- keep these despite the rules above ---
# Checksums and READMEs are small, and they are how a fresh clone verifies
# that its re-downloaded data matches what we actually analysed.
!**/CHECKSUMS.sha256
!**/data/**/README.md
!**/data/**/*.py
!**/data/**/*.R
**/docs/supplementary_figures*.txt
